# Bounds the source context `gcloud builds submit` uploads. Terraform's container module runs
# `gcloud builds submit --config docker/cloudbuild.yaml .` from the repo root. The Docker build COPYs
# the uv lockfiles (.python-version, pyproject.toml, uv.lock) and reads docker/, so the context needs
# exactly those — nothing else. Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which does NOT
# exclude src/, notebooks/, configs/, etc., uploading far more than the build needs. This is the ONLY
# gcloud source-upload path in the repo (the seed job uploads src/ via Terraform's archive_file, not
# gcloud), so scoping to just the build inputs is safe.
*
!/docker
!/docker/**
!/.python-version
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.lock
